                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "background": 1,
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "id": "obj-42",
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 490.0, 540.0, 235.0, 21.0 ],
                                                    "text": "Resonant band-pass filter in Gen container"
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "background": 1,
                                                    "id": "obj-43",
                                                    "linecount": 4,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 490.0, 560.0, 350.0, 64.0 ],
                                                    "text": "To perform the filtering, we've implemented a resonant band-pass filter in a Gen container. Gen allows for creating low dsp tasks such as filters with maximum accuracy, and implement one's own filter formulas under patching or dsp code forms."
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "background": 1,
                                                    "id": "obj-33",
                                                    "linecount": 5,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 60.0, 40.0, 710.0, 78.0 ],
                                                    "text": "The modulation signal is used to read in filter data stored in a named buffer, through a lookup table (the sample~ object). Each lookup table represents one of the five voice formants. Buffers have a size of 5 samples, and each sample slot has a center frequency, linear amplitude and Q factor stored, representing one formant of one vowel - u, o, a, a and i. The sample~ object understands a [0. 1.] normalized signal and interpolates sample values with intermediate control signal values. This results in smooth filter transitions between each vowel. Additionally, frequencies, amplitudes and Qs can be scaled for further audio tweaks."
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "background": 1,
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "id": "obj-15",
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 60.0, 20.0, 82.0, 21.0 ],
                                                    "text": "Formant filter"
                                                }
                                            },
