                                    "patching_rect": [ 310.0, 330.0, 44.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "Mod R"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-10",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 220.0, 330.0, 42.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "Mod L"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-42",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 670.0, 540.0, 183.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "Band-pass filter in Gen container"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-43",
                                    "linecount": 5,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 670.0, 560.0, 273.0, 78.0 ],
                                    "text": "To perform the filtering, we've implemented a band-pass filter in a Gen container. Gen allows for creating low dsp tasks such as filters with maximum accuracy, and implementing one's own filter formulas in patching or dsp code forms."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-30",
                                    "linecount": 6,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 670.0, 440.0, 250.0, 93.0 ],
                                    "text": "We now need to map the [0. 1.] modulation signal to our filter frequency range [200. 2000.], expressed in Herz. This can be easily achieved using the scale~ object, which also includes a power coefficient to control the sharpness of the mapping."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-26",
                                    "linecount": 10,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 670.0, 290.0, 253.0, 150.0 ],
                                    "text": "To obtain stereo modulation, we need to shift the action of the modulation for one of the audio channels, when the Spread parameter is engaged. To do that, we're passing the modulation signals through two triangular waveform tables. If we then shift the input phase of the triangle~ object of the right channel as we increase the value of Spread, the modulation of both channels will get more and more out of phase."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-24",
                                    "linecount": 7,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 670.0, 180.0, 263.0, 107.0 ],
                                    "text": "In auto mode, the modulation is produced in response to the estimation of the amplitude envelope of the input sound. Typically, envelope following is obtained with signal amplitude averaging (the average~ object in this patch) followed by some filtering or smoothing of the signal (the slide~ object in this patch)."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                    "linecount": 5,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 670.0, 100.0, 240.0, 78.0 ],
                                    "text": "In manual mode, the Manual parameter is used as a modulation control of the cutoff frequency of a band-pass filter, which passes frequencies within a certain range and rejects frequencies outside that range."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-4",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 180.0, 603.0, 91.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "Band-pass filter"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "bubble": 1,
                                    "bubbleside": 3,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "fontsize": 11.0,
